.TH "SLIPWAY-DIFF" "1" "2026-09-30" "slipway 0.1.0" "Slipway Manual"
.SH NAME
slipway\-diff \- Show where projects differ from their manifests
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY "slipway diff"
.I "[NAME... | project/NAME...]"\&
.RI [ flags ]
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show where each selected project differs from its manifest.
.PP
Compares every project of the current group, the projects named, the ones a label selector matches, or with \-\-all\-groups every project, with its manifest. Each project that differs prints its name and one line per difference: Missing, Remote, Branch, Revision or Behind, then the blocker that keeps sync from fast\-forwarding the branch, if any. A line is followed by the git command that shows or resolves it when there is one; slipway never runs it. A project that matches its manifest prints nothing.
.PP
The repositories are read as they are on disk: diff contacts no remote and writes nothing, so Behind is as of the last fetch, which slipway fetch refreshes. A project pinned by spec.revision is compared with that commit instead of its upstream, and is blocked when the repository lacks the commit, HEAD is past it or its upstream does not hold it. A paused or FetchOnly project shows a blocker only when git cannot read its repository.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-selector\fR \fIEXPR\fR
Selector (label query) to filter on, supports '=', '==', '!=', 'in', 'notin' (e.g. \-l key1=value1,key2=value2,key3 in (value3)). Matching objects must satisfy all of the specified label constraints.
.TP
\fB\-A\fR, \fB\-\-all\-groups\fR
If present, compare every project across all groups with its manifest. The group in the current configuration is ignored even if specified with \-\-group.
.SH DRIFT
.TP
\fBMissing\fR
The registered path is relative or is not a directory. For a path that is not a directory, a project with spec.remote shows the git clone command that recreates it.
.TP
\fBRemote\fR
origin is absent or differs from spec.remote. Sync never changes a remote.
.TP
\fBBranch\fR
HEAD is detached or on another branch than spec.branch. Sync never switches branches.
.TP
\fBRevision\fR
HEAD is not the commit spec.revision pins. The pin replaces the upstream, so a pinned project is never Behind; under FastForward sync will fast\-forward a branch behind the pin to it unless a blocker stops it, and never moves a branch back.
.TP
\fBBehind\fR
The checked\-out branch is behind its upstream. Under FastForward sync will fast\-forward it unless a blocker stops it; under FetchOnly, or while spec.paused is true, it is only reported.
.SH BLOCKERS
A blocker says why the checked\-out branch cannot be fast\-forwarded, onto its upstream or, for a project pinned by spec.revision, onto the pin. The first three mean git could not read the repository and apply to every project; the others apply only under FastForward to a project that is not paused, and RevisionNotFound, PastRevision and OffUpstream only to a pinned one.
.TP
\fBNotARepo\fR
The directory exists but holds no repository.
.TP
\fBUnsafe\fR
git refused the repository because another user owns it (safe.directory); the git command that trusts it follows.
.TP
\fBUnknown\fR
git could not answer; the reason is also printed once on stderr.
.TP
\fBDetached\fR
HEAD points at a commit rather than a branch.
.TP
\fBUnborn\fR
The branch has no commits yet.
.TP
\fBGone\fR
The upstream is configured but its ref no longer exists.
.TP
\fBNoUpstream\fR
The branch tracks no upstream.
.TP
\fBRevisionNotFound\fR
The repository has no commit by the name spec.revision pins.
.TP
\fBPastRevision\fR
HEAD is past the pinned commit or on another line of history, so reaching the pin would move the branch back.
.TP
\fBOffUpstream\fR
The upstream does not hold the pinned commit, which may be on another branch or a fork; sync moves a branch only along its upstream.
.TP
\fBConflicted\fR
The branch is behind and the working tree has unmerged paths.
.TP
\fBDirty\fR
The branch is behind and has staged or unstaged changes; untracked files do not block.
.TP
\fBDiverged\fR
The branch is behind and has commits of its own.
.TP
\fBInProgress\fR
The branch would be fast\-forwarded, but a merge, rebase, cherry\-pick, revert, bisect or git am is in progress.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
\fB0\fR
Every selected project matches its manifest.
.TP
\fB1\fR
Runtime error, such as a missing resource or an unreadable manifest, or a project whose state is Unknown because git failed or did not finish.
.TP
\fB2\fR
Usage error: unknown command, unknown flag or invalid argument.
.TP
\fB3\fR
At least one selected project differs from its manifest or is blocked, including a directory that holds no repository (NotARepo) and a repository git refuses (Unsafe).
.TP
\fB130\fR
Interrupted by SIGINT.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
# Show where the projects of the current group differ from their manifests
slipway diff
.EE
.PP
.EX
# Show every project that differs, in every group
slipway diff \-A
.EE
.PP
.EX
# Compare two projects of the work group
slipway diff api web \-n work
.EE
.PP
.EX
# Compare the projects labeled lang=rust
slipway diff \-l lang=rust
.EE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
